Translate the process into observable facility requirements (@cm-facility-brief: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X", #source "../sources/Contamination-Control-Engineering-NASA.lingua#r_2XKKPYTW2DPQPQZ8VPV23BJ8A5", #clean-manufacturing "Map-people-material-product-and-waste-through-the-layout.lingua#r_129VQ3R7CAJVEXHTC7PT61KD1H") { r_38A200F1H46XAJ3DRTKHZ183SV
**Read:** [Cleanroom programming and energy — Tschudi, Sartor and Xu](../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X), architectural programming and section 2.2.2; [Contamination control engineering — Tribble and colleagues, NASA CR 4740](../sources/Contamination-Control-Engineering-NASA.lingua#r_2XKKPYTW2DPQPQZ8VPV23BJ8A5), functional contamination effects.

Start with an object and its use: an optical surface, a patterned structure, a culture or an assembled mechanism. Identify which material, quantity, location and exposure history can compromise that use. A room classification records a particular property under stated conditions; it does not specify every chemical, biological, thermal or mechanical requirement.

Connect a proposed limit to a measurement and a consequence. Separate established process evidence, a provisional engineering assumption and a future growth allowance. Their uncertainty has different implications for design.

**Work:** Write a short process account with a sensitive area, operating states, contamination mechanisms and measurable outcomes. Trace each proposed facility requirement to that account. Compare protecting the whole room with protecting a smaller region without silently transferring dirt, heat or maintenance difficulty elsewhere.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
**Continue in clean manufacturing:** [Map people, material, product and waste through the layout](Map-people-material-product-and-waste-through-the-layout.lingua#r_129VQ3R7CAJVEXHTC7PT61KD1H).

